## Define and load property
      - we write it in property file and use @PropertySource to load it in env default property source is application.property
      - and use @Value to use it
      - location of app.prop
            - classpath root src/resource etc
      - also have profile specific prop file like prod,dev,test -> app-dev.prop
      - also use yml file app.yml here space have 2 indentation from parent
      - multiple profile related data also store in single file by spring.profile property also use --- which indicates separate logic file

      - Precedence
            highest is devtool and test property because it need to override default and actual
            lowest is default in application.property
            1) devtool setting 2) @TestPropertySource and @SpringBootTest 3) command line argument 4) spring apk json 5) servlet config / context
            6) JNDI attribute from java:comp|env 7) java systeam prop 8) os env var 9)profile specific app.prop 10)app prop 11)@PropertySource file 12) apk default prop

      - map property to your class by using @ConfigurationProperties
            - @Value("${prop key}") String user;
            - we need to repeat prefix here like abc.xyz.user , abc.xyz.pass etc to overcome this 
                  create class which have annotation @ConfigurationProperties(prefix="abc.xyz") which have field like String user , String pass
                  - for make this happen we need to create a bean of it by
                        - @EnableConfigurationProperties on apk class
                        - @ConfigurationPropertyScan on apk or @Component on property class it self
            - Relexed binding
                  -  @ConfigurationProperties(prefix="sagar-desai") matches sagarDesai , sagar-desai ,sagar_desai,SAGAR_DESAi




